{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"d77be8de8141783a57abdaa2802406cb344438ca1b3076ea0a76e9f91c12d9a8","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_4040fe47c9c5791b11bbfd85bfaa69d24eb9f030f5e0d34869aef0c0b4910f3d","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to neural network architectures for tree-structured decoding. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact documentation, as no venue-specific policies or external overlap data are available. The paper does not contain a dedicated ethics or broader impact section, nor does it explicitly detail data licensing or consent protocols for the user-generated IFTTT dataset, though it cites the source.","paper_id":"HkYhZDqxg","paper_identity_sha256":"5a159e71cd5cbf373fefeb04ac41db07125f38f43a8e527836eb80017b516a3b","prompt_identity_sha256":"f378319f06005c98b6dda8c2190a0a6b84387d20e474a733d86fc02fcaebdd15","raw_response_sha256":"a188fa8dfcf57f0d9472ada2489d7751981066c79f1aa14a39c61584708b5241","request_identity_sha256":"a8dd40050d2250ce4383e5fdbb86893dd8c2d1c00c7b0b8f3eda2e86ea0f7ad4","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"e5c968c94a6d82629fa48acdb237b3df81e8c4c0674680fd905b9ae5f123f074","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section discussing ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the proposed tree-structured decoding architecture. The application to mapping natural language to functional programs (IFTTT recipes) is a standard NLP task, and no specific dual-use or safety concerns are raised or mitigated in the text. The absence of such discussion is noted, but no specific ethical violation is evident from the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the IFTTT dataset, which is described as 'user-generated' and 'crawled from the IFTTT website' (Quirk et al., 2015). The text does not explicitly state the licensing terms, consent mechanisms, or privacy compliance measures regarding the use of this user-generated data. While the data is cited from a prior publication, the paper does not provide specific evidence of adherence to data privacy regulations or licensing restrictions for the crawled content.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper header explicitly lists the authors' names ('David Alvarez-Melis & Tommi S. Jaakkola'), their affiliation ('Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Lab MIT'), and their email addresses ('{davidam, tommi}@csail.mit.edu'). While this is standard for published versions, in the context of a double-blind review submission, such visible identifiers would typically constitute an anonymity violation. However, without a frozen venue policy confirming the specific anonymity requirements for this submission instance, this is noted as a visible identifier rather than a confirmed policy breach.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not include external plagiarism checks, overlap analysis, or information regarding dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work (e.g., Dong & Lapata, 2016; Zhang et al., 2016) and presents a novel architecture. There is no visible evidence of uncredited reuse or simultaneous submission in the text provided. The absence of evidence does not prove originality or the absence of dual submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. The 'Discussion and Future Work' section focuses on technical extensions (e.g., machine translation) rather than societal implications. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for this venue/year, the absence is noted as a lack of visible compliance documentation rather than a violation.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"1555fac5375fff54689759a7468ec7b44eb30ea72fd1890e9a9a68bea8648aaf","paper_id":"HkYhZDqxg","paper_ordinal":94,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"a188fa8dfcf57f0d9472ada2489d7751981066c79f1aa14a39c61584708b5241","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"HkYhZDqxg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"31d17778737b15b8bb786b9a7c6dcc1dc50558f4a8b1d9bc20f42f0c8d3a5e75","request_identity_sha256":"a8dd40050d2250ce4383e5fdbb86893dd8c2d1c00c7b0b8f3eda2e86ea0f7ad4","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":789,"prompt_tokens":17567,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18356},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"a8dd40050d2250ce4383e5fdbb86893dd8c2d1c00c7b0b8f3eda2e86ea0f7ad4","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}